.\" Warden man page
.TH WARDEN 1 "2026-03-16" "1.0.0" "Warden Manual"
.SH NAME
warden \- describe the system you live in
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B warden
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Warden captures your development environment \(em git identities, SSH configs,
system packages, and developer tools \(em into a single config file. Switch
identities, snapshot installed software, apply configs to a fresh machine, back
everything up into portable archives, and maintain your system with integrated
cleanup tools.
.PP
Configuration is stored in
.B warden.jsonc
(JSON5 with comments and trailing commas). Warden searches the following
locations in order:
.RS
.IP 1. 3
\fB~/.warden/warden.jsonc\fR
.IP 2. 3
\fB~/.ssh/warden.jsonc\fR
.IP 3. 3
\fB~/warden.jsonc\fR
.IP 4. 3
\fB./warden.jsonc\fR
.RE
.PP
Use
.B \-c PATH
to override with an explicit config file.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS "Identity (warden id)"
.TP
.B id switch \fItarget\fR
Apply a git identity from config. Sets user.name, user.email, user.signingkey,
core.sshCommand, gpg.format, and commit.gpgsign globally.
.TP
.B id list
List all identity targets defined in the config.
.TP
.B id show \fR[\fItarget\fR]
Show the current git identity, or a specific target's config if \fItarget\fR is
given.
.SS "Packages (warden pkg)"
.TP
.B pkg scan
Scan the system for installed packages and developer tools, then update the
packages and tools sections in warden.jsonc.
.TP
.B pkg apply \fR[\fB\-f\fR|\fB\-\-force\fR]
Install packages and developer tools from config. Already-installed items are
skipped unless \fB\-\-force\fR is used.
.TP
.B pkg install \fIMANAGER\fB:\fIPKG\fR [\fIMANAGER\fB:\fIPKG\fR ...]
Install packages using manager:package syntax. Run with no arguments to see
available managers and their install status.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-save
Also add installed packages to warden.jsonc.
.TP
.B \-\-any
Bypass OS platform check (allow any manager).
.RE
.SS "Backup (warden backup)"
.TP
.B backup \fR[\fB\-m\fR \fIMODULES\fR] [\fB\-o\fR \fIFILE\fR] [\fB\-\-skip\-scan\fR] [\fB\-\-include\-missing\fR]
Backup selected modules into a tar.gz archive. \fIMODULES\fR is a
comma-separated list of: \fBgit\fR (identities + signing keys), \fBssh\fR
(SSH config + identity keys), \fBpkg\fR (packages + tools). Use \fBall\fR
as shorthand for all modules. Defaults to \fBall\fR.
.PP
When the \fBpkg\fR module is included, system packages are re-scanned
automatically before archiving. Use \fB\-\-skip\-scan\fR to disable this.
.RS
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-scan
Skip re-scanning system packages before backup.
.TP
.B \-\-include\-missing
Include SSH hosts whose key files are missing on disk.
.TP
.B \-o \fIFILE\fR
Output archive path (default: auto-generated with date).
.RE
.SS "Restore (warden restore)"
.TP
.B restore \fR[\fB\-m\fR \fIMODULES\fR] \fIarchive\fR
Restore selected modules from a backup archive. \fIMODULES\fR is a
comma-separated list of: \fBgit\fR, \fBssh\fR, \fBpkg\fR, or \fBall\fR.
Defaults to \fBall\fR.
Exits with an error if the archive does not contain a requested module.
.SS "Maintenance (warden mole)"
System cleanup and optimization powered by
.BR Mole " (" tw93/mole ")."
Mole is auto-installed via Homebrew if not found on the system.
.TP
.B mole clean
Deep system cleanup \(em removes app caches, browser caches, developer tool
caches, system logs, and temporary files.
.TP
.B mole optimize
System optimization \(em rebuilds system databases, resets network services,
refreshes Finder/Dock, cleans diagnostic logs.
.TP
.B mole analyze \fR[\fIpath\fR]
Visual disk space explorer with interactive navigation. Pass a path to analyze
a specific directory.
.TP
.B mole status \fR[\fB\-\-json\fR]
Real-time system health dashboard showing CPU, memory, disk, power, network,
and an overall health score. Use \fB\-\-json\fR for machine-readable output.
.PP
For additional Mole features not exposed through warden (uninstall, purge,
installer, touchid), run the
.B mo
command directly:
.RS
.nf
mo              # interactive menu
mo uninstall    # smart app uninstaller
mo purge        # clean build artifacts (node_modules, target, etc.)
mo installer    # find and remove .dmg/.pkg/.zip installers
mo touchid      # configure Touch ID for sudo
.fi
.RE
.PP
See
.UR https://github.com/tw93/mole
.UE
for full documentation.
.SS "System"
.TP
.B update \fR[\fIbranch\fR]
Self-update warden by pulling latest from git and reinstalling. Defaults to the
current branch.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c \fIPATH\fR
Override the config file path.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Preview changes without writing to disk. Supported by all mutating commands.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored output. Equivalent to setting \fBWARDEN_NO_COLOR=1\fR.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B WARDEN_NO_COLOR
Set to \fB1\fR, \fBtrue\fR, or \fByes\fR to disable colored output. The
standard \fBNO_COLOR\fR variable is also respected.
.TP
.B WARDEN_USE_CN
Set to \fB1\fR, \fBtrue\fR, or \fByes\fR to route downloads through
China-accessible mirrors (Homebrew via USTC, PyPI via Aliyun, Rust via
rsproxy.cn, Node/npm via npmmirror.com, GitHub via ghp.ci).
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.warden/warden.jsonc
Primary config file location.
.TP
.B ~/.warden/keys/
Directory where backup-restored signing keys are stored.
.TP
.B ~/.ssh/config
SSH config file that the \fBssh\fR module operates on during backup and restore.
.SH SUPPORTED PACKAGE MANAGERS
brew, cask, mas, apt, dnf, pacman, apk, snap, flatpak, cargo, npm, pnpm, pipx,
and developer tools (rustup, node, pnpm, go, etc.).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Error (config not found, archive invalid, installation failure, etc.).
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
# Snapshot your system
warden pkg scan

# Switch git identity
warden id switch personal

# Install packages from config
warden pkg apply

# Backup everything (default)
warden backup -o ~/backup.tar.gz

# Backup only git identities and packages
warden backup -m git,pkg

# Backup without re-scanning packages
warden backup --skip-scan

# Restore on a new machine
warden restore ~/backup.tar.gz

# Restore only packages from an archive
warden restore -m pkg ~/backup.tar.gz

# Clean up the system
warden mole clean

# Check system health
warden mole status
.fi
